Paired-end QC/trimming completed locally with fastp 1.3.6.

Inputs:
  data/inputs/raw_reads/pair/forward/forward.fastqsanger.gz
  data/inputs/raw_reads/pair/reverse/reverse.fastqsanger.gz

Processing:
  Mate-overlap adapter trimming only (no adapter sequence and no
  --detect_adapter_for_pe autodetection pass).
  Filters: Q<20 low-quality threshold; reject if >40% low-quality bases,
  >5 Ns, or post-trim length <15 in either mate.
  Other trimming/correction disabled: --disable_trim_poly_g; no quality
  window trimming, poly-X trimming, UMI processing, merging, or correction.

Result:
  Input pairs: 377961
  Retained synchronized pairs: 277113
  Adapter-trimmed reads: 89226; adapter-trimmed bases: 2091846
  fastp failed reads: low quality 201676; too many Ns 20; too short 0

Validation:
  gzip integrity passed for both outputs; each has 277113 records.
  Mate IDs/order and sequence/quality lengths match. Retained read lengths
  range from 31 to 101 bases; all requested per-read thresholds passed.

Outputs:
  final_answer/trimmed_forward.fastqsanger.gz
  final_answer/trimmed_reverse.fastqsanger.gz
